  "raw_text": "arbecue rib compare to your favorite Arby's brisket sandwich? What's better or worse about it? User: I like the way it's cooked. It has a little sauce on it. I'm not a big on sauce on my meat. I like to add sauce as I need it when I'm eating. I don't really care for it to be on my meat, but the way they cook the ribs are very tender, and it's just the way they cook it. Agent: That sounds delicious. Do you have one more similar item you like from any chain, and how does it compare to your favorite Arby's brisket sandwich? User: Let me see. I like... Agent: No problem, take your time. User: Okay. I'm trying to decide because, like I said, I have... I like chicken nuggets or McDonald's. I like their chicken nuggets. And what I like about it is that it's individual pieces and they taste like real meat. So I like them compared to the brisket. It's not better than the brisket for me, but if I had to have a choice, I would choose the brisket over the McDonald's chicken nuggets. Agent: Thank y",
